{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm] [F] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
King [Bb]Zedekiah made a covenant with all the [Eb]people
To [Gm7]proclaim liber[F/A]ty for every He[Bb]brew slave
[F/A]The of[Gm7]ficials and the crowd [F]who entered the [Eb]pact
Obeyed the [Gm7]word and [F/A]set their brothers [Bb]free
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But you turned back and profaned my [F]name
Took back the men [Gm7]and women you had re[Eb]leased
I made a [Bb]covenant with your fathers long a[F]go
But you did not [Eb]listen to the [F]voice of the [Bb]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
